From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:26:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] fate/filter-video: test the dibr filter

A test picture with a near disc that moves over a far ramp: the default
path, the middle view with backward warping and the depth-aided fill,
layered warping with Telea's fill, the smoothing with no fill, 12-bit
4:4:4 with a 16-bit depth map at half the size, and the Stereo 3D side
data of the output; and the samples: the depth map and the parallax map
of mpegts/depth-aux.ts read from their supplemental information, and the
depth auxiliary layer of hevc/depth-layer.hevc with its depth
representation information.

The tests need FFmpeg configured with --enable-libstereodibr.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
